=====================================================================

TSTAT is a command line program that will display the current TIPI status
by default.  It will also display the current configuration, halt, reset,
and update the RPi. For use with Geneve OS/MDOS version 7.30 and above.


USAGE:
=======
TSTAT is run from the Geneve OS command line or batch file:

               TSTAT <optional parameter>

      Options: TSTAT C   - Show PI.CONFIG
               TSTAT H   - Halt the Raspberry PI (PI.SHUTDOWN)
               TSTAT R   - Restart the Raspberry PI (PI.RESTART)
               TSTAT S   - Show PI.STATUS
               TSTAT U   - Force upgrade (PI.UPGRADE)
               TSTAT E   - Display the EPROM version date/time stamp
               TSTAT ?   - show options

       The upgrade and restart options wait for the operation to complete.
       A "spinner" is displayed until the TIPI card senses the RPi is ready.


